For LCP - optimizing the actual largest content element directly:

<img
  src="hero-optimized.webp"
  loading="eager"        // the LCP element should NOT be lazy-loaded,
                            // since it needs to appear as early as possible
  fetchpriority="high"   // explicitly tells the browser this is a
                            // high-priority resource, loaded ahead of
                            // less critical images on the page
  width="1200" height="600"
/>

For CLS - reserving layout space BEFORE content actually loads in,
directly preventing the late-arriving-content shift lesson 1 diagnosed:

<img src="ad-banner.jpg" width="728" height="90" />
// Explicit width/height reserves this EXACT space immediately,
// even before the image itself has finished loading, preventing
// surrounding content from shifting once it does arrive

For INP - directly applying Module 14, lesson 4's memoization
specifically where the Profiler has shown a genuinely slow re-render
is the actual cause of sluggish interaction response:

const ExpensiveList = React.memo(function ExpensiveList({ items }: Props) {
  // ... only re-renders when items genuinely changes, directly
  // reducing the delay between an interaction and the next paint
  // IF this component was genuinely identified as the bottleneck
});

